W: 1. Fortune, my foe, why dost thou frown on me?
W: And will thy favours never greater be?
W: Wilt thou, I say, forever breed my pain?
W: And will thou ne'er restore my joys againe?
W:
W: 2. Fortune hath wrought me grief and great annoy;
W: Fortune hath falsely stolen my love away.
W: My love and joy whose sight did make me glad;
W: Such great misfortunes never young man had.
